From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:55:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Assert on the IEJoin semi join's conditions without an assert-only binding

IEJoinLocalSourceState::ResolveSemiJoin() binds the join conditions to
a reference that only D_ASSERT() reads, so in a release build, where
D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, -Wunused-variable reports it. The
assertion reads the conditions from the operator itself; upstream
later reads the binding in the join's tail selection.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp
index 3a8150f69e..bb85cd5e69 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp
@@ -1297,8 +1297,7 @@ void IEJoinLocalSourceState::ResolveInnerJoin(ExecutionContext &context, DataChu
 
 void IEJoinLocalSourceState::ResolveSemiJoin(ExecutionContext &context, DataChunk &result) {
 	auto &op = gsource.op;
-	const auto &conditions = op.conditions;
-	D_ASSERT(conditions.size() == 2);
+	D_ASSERT(op.conditions.size() == 2);
 
 	auto &ie_sink = op.sink_state->Cast<IEJoinGlobalState>();
 	auto &left_table = *ie_sink.tables[0];
